<title>AUSTRALIA: APN half-year net profit rises.</title>
<headline>APN half-year net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>		     (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    21.06 vs 18.35</p>
<p>    Net				     14.40 vs 11.56</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     3.70 vs  3.50</p>
<p>    Sales				  129.19 vs 120.78</p>
<p>    Other income			  10.03 vs   8.88</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    6.2  vs   5.5</p>
<p>    Abnormal			  loss 1.27 vs loss 1.66</p>
<p>    Tax					3.67 vs   3.98</p>
<p>    Interest				 8.65 vs   8.47</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   4.59 vs   3.15</p>
<p>    Minorities			     1.72 vs   1.16</p>
<p> Dividend is 100 pct franked</p>
<p> Pay date Oct 6</p>
<p> Reg date Sep 19</p>
<p>NOTE: Australian Provincial Newspapers Holdings Ltd (APN) is a regional newspaper publisher and radio operator and is about 49 percent owned by Irish businessman Tony O'Reilly through family interests and his main newspaper group, Independent Newspapers Plc.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
